From c37c95299a1c73baf9cdc43a3375870ca231d8f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carter Chen <carter.chen.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Dec 2025 08:46:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fw_update: Reimplement package parser to use new libpldm API

libpldm has revised the APIs for firmware package, the old APIs are
now deprecated. Switch to the new APIs and use libpldm iterators to
ensure compatibility with the latest libpldm version and PLDM fw
update pkg v1.3.0

Since the reimplemented processPackage() no longer delegates to
processStream(), it raises updateInProgress itself once the Activation
and ActivationProgress objects exist. Upstream only sets that flag in
processStream() and activatePackage() returns early without it, so
without this a package dropped into the firmware update watch
directory would stay in Activating forever and the update would never
start.

- Build Yosemite V4: Pass
- Firmware update Yosemite V4 PLDM components: Pass

Change-Id: I56106c66b61167bae8398c8616c376941097c627
Signed-off-by: Unive Tien <unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Carter Chen <carter.chen.wiwynn@gmail.com>
